00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:01.956
Two technologies sit at the center of this modernization.

00:45:02.596 --> 00:45:08.316
The first is AI. AI is helping us make
better decisions on how we deploy people,

00:45:08.756 --> 00:45:12.636
how we process information, and how we respond to incidents.

00:45:13.236 --> 00:45:18.916
The second is robotics. Robotics takes
on repetitive, physical, demanding,

00:45:18.916 --> 00:45:23.156
higher risk tasks that are often so
that our officers can really focus on.

00:45:23.156 --> 00:45:27.236
Work that requires judgment, requires empathy

00:45:27.356 --> 00:45:35.076
and human interaction to make all these things
work together. We have built Mozart on AWS.

00:45:37.036 --> 00:45:41.756
Mozart brings together data from sensors, from cameras, from robots,

00:45:42.116 --> 00:45:48.316
from operational systems into a single view so
that our operators can really see what is happening

00:45:48.596 --> 00:45:52.396
and be able to respond quickly. Behind the scenes

00:45:52.396 --> 00:45:56.676
Mozart uses Amazon Bedrock to power its AI reasoning.

00:45:57.156 --> 00:46:03.836
This gives the agents the ability to understand the context,
to make decisions, to learn from past incidents,

00:46:04.076 --> 00:46:08.076
and to communicate naturally, just like you saw from Max.

00:46:11.156 --> 00:46:15.276
On top of that sits Mozart multi-agent orchestration layer.

00:46:15.516 --> 00:46:20.316
And this is where we've developed a whole
suite of AI agents that are working together.

00:46:20.316 --> 00:46:23.916
The first of it is CFO. CFO is our computer vision agent,

00:46:24.356 --> 00:46:31.876
which is using computer models trained on Amazon SageMaker
to really detect over 20 types of security incidents, for example,

00:46:31.916 --> 00:46:37.916
unattended bags. The second is intelligent IQ,
which is our large language model.

00:46:38.116 --> 00:46:44.756
Oxygen. And this helps our human officers
actually generate and submit reports up to 30% faster.

00:46:45.156 --> 00:46:49.516
And finally we have the AERORL, which is the reinforcement agent.

00:46:49.716 --> 00:46:58.836
And this helps to roster which of our human officers to manage
what tasks, when to escalate to human operators and how to respond.

00:47:00.636 --> 00:47:03.236
Now we don't use AI just to generate insights.

00:47:03.716 --> 00:47:09.676
We use it actually to orchestrate decisions
in our operations, to coordinate resources,

00:47:09.676 --> 00:47:14.156
and to drive action in the real world so that operators can trust.

00:47:14.876 --> 00:47:17.436
Our customers are not just asking what AI can do.

00:47:18.076 --> 00:47:26.356
They're asking how all these systems are secured on safety and security,
against breaches, against manipulation and against failures.

00:47:27.476 --> 00:47:30.716
Cyber security is not separate from AI.

00:47:30.916 --> 00:47:38.356
It is foundational, and we've recently started building our AI agents
built for cyber security based on Amazon Bedrock.

00:47:39.476 --> 00:47:43.476
And another important area in operations context is trust.

00:47:43.516 --> 00:47:47.836
Trust by the operators. What matters is not just that it works.

00:47:48.356 --> 00:47:50.876
Our operators must be able to trust it.

00:47:51.036 --> 00:47:56.396
They must be able to understand it,
respond accordingly for it to operate reliably.

00:47:59.796 --> 00:48:04.156
So today we deploy many different types
of robots across different environments.

00:48:04.596 --> 00:48:10.036
We have real enforcement and deterrent robots like MAXINE and MAX M1.

00:48:10.836 --> 00:48:14.636
And we also have humanoid concierge
like MAX that you just saw just now.

00:48:14.636 --> 00:48:20.076
And we also have autonomous quadrupeds like Eve, which are robot dogs.

00:48:20.356 --> 00:48:24.836
And now that you’ve seen MAX, I would like to introduce you to ACE.

00:48:37.236 --> 00:48:38.596
Thank you everyone.

00:48:39.636 --> 00:48:41.956
I'll make sure I'll get out of the way.

00:48:41.956 --> 00:48:46.516
So meet ACE, everyone. ACE is our autonomous canine explorer.

00:48:47.316 --> 00:48:51.556
It extends our operational reach in frontline security environments.

00:48:52.116 --> 00:49:00.316
ACE patrols autonomously in large,
complex environments, and it detects anomalies via vision models.

00:49:00.916 --> 00:49:06.996
And these feed into Mozart. And then the system decides
in real time how to respond.

00:49:07.636 --> 00:49:14.996
And that's the power of having robots,
AI agents and humans working on one single platform.

00:49:17.916 --> 00:49:23.316
So now you've seen two different robots on this same stage,
different forms, different jobs,

00:49:23.316 --> 00:49:27.636
but both are connected to the same platform and cloud infrastructure.

00:49:30.556 --> 00:49:37.836
And that's the real story here. It's not just about any single robot,
but it's really about the system behind it.

00:49:38.116 --> 00:49:41.476
And this is why building with AWS matters.

00:49:41.916 --> 00:49:44.796
AWS has given us more than just infrastructure.

00:49:45.116 --> 00:49:52.516
They've given us the foundation to build,
to test, to train, to deploy and to continuously improve.

00:49:53.356 --> 00:50:00.000
And the ability to scale a new generation of AI
powered operational technologies. At Certis

